  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added a source-transparent packed GF(p)[x] extended Euclidean kernel with Sage-normalized monic outputs and a single transactional output layout. The kernel copies inputs into compiler-owned scratch, so compiled callers may safely overlap input and output typed views; zero/zero returns Sage's (0, 0, 0). Complete 32-bit primality and canonical-residue checks, verified leading-coefficient inverses, and strict Euclidean degree-decrease checks reject malformed domains without hanging. Focused compiled, dynamic Sage.js, and CPython tests cover Sage fixtures, randomized Bezout identities, the largest 32-bit prime, composite/nonunit moduli, noncanonical residues, zero and nonmonic constants, aliasing, and transactional rejection. On the measured AMD EPYC 7B13 host, compiled same-source XGCD is faster than public FLINT through degree 128 and slower at degree 256; dynamic same-source execution remains a correctness fallback.",
    "risks": [
      "The public PolynomialElement.xgcd method is intentionally not wired in this write-disjoint lane.",
      "The kernel uses classical quadratic polynomial arithmetic; the measured compiled-source/public-FLINT crossover bracket of degree 128 to 256 is specific to one Linux x64 host and must become dispatch-profile evidence rather than a hard-coded universal threshold.",
      "The broad pnpm test:changed gate is blocked by integration-only registration of this focused test in test/node-test-manifest.cjs, plus unrelated baseline GF(2) packed shift/module-surface failures and a noisy uint64 structural performance ratio of 4.84 above its 4.0 gate.",
      "The full pnpm test:native gate completed compiler, FFI, lifecycle, sanitizer, and native-kernel suites, then failed in unchanged test/dense-prime-migration.cjs because strictEqual compared actual 0n with expected 0."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "In the integration lane, add src/lib/sagejs/polynomial_algorithms/packed_prime_xgcd.py to pyrightconfig.json and test/packed-prime-polynomial-xgcd.cjs to test/node-test-manifest.cjs; explicit Pyright already reports zero errors.",
      "Obtain a fresh independent review of domain proofs, degree progress, transactional publication, typed-view aliasing, and the benchmark comparison before public wiring.",
      "After review, wire the public polynomial surface with the one-output ABI and dispatch compiled source only within a multi-host measured profile, retaining declared/public FLINT for larger degrees."
    ]
  }
